---
/*
  One page about the person behind the shelf. Replace the copy; the shape --
  what you make, how you work, how to reach you -- is what the theme is for.
*/
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHead from '../components/PageHead.astro';
import { contact, site } from '../config';

const description = `${site.author} builds small web tools and writes down what happens.`;
---

<Base title="About" {description}>
  <PageHead title="About" lead={description} />

  <section class="border-border border-t">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-wide px-4 py-12 md:py-16">
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          I build small web tools, usually to solve something that annoyed me first. Most of them
          stay small on purpose: a status page that fits in one browser tab, a backup schedule that
          tells you when it did not run, a script that turns a folder of invoices into a table.
        </p>
        <p>
          Everything I have shipped is on the <a href="/work">work</a> page, including the things I
          have since switched off. A product that stopped being worth running is not a failure worth
          hiding; the page keeps it, marked archived, with the note explaining what replaced it.
        </p>
        <h2>How I work</h2>
        <p>
          One project at a time, in the open, with the boring parts written down as I go. The{' '}
          <a href="/notes">notes</a> are that record: what a decision cost, what I would do
          differently, what the bill looked like at the end of the month.
        </p>
        <h2>Elsewhere</h2>
        <p>
          The fastest way to reach me is email:{' '}
          <a href={`mailto:${contact.email}`}>{contact.email}</a>. There is also a{' '}
          <a href="/contact">contact page</a>, and the site has an <a href="/rss.xml">RSS feed</a>{' '}
          if you would rather have the notes come to you.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
